        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Description: Plain weave cotton, drawn thread work, needlewoven bars and embroidered metal thread, faced with block printed cotton.\nFacing for a bodice. White cotton with drawn thread work and needlewoven bars in red silk forming horizontal, vertical and diagonal lines.  Where these meet silver and silver-gilt threads have been embroidered to form small roundels; the type of metal thread alternates."@en , "part, embroidered net, 1800s, Persian"@en ;
